       <div class="ch"><h1>Inverting Amplifier</h1><div class="ch-card"><h2>How it works</h2><ul><li><strong>R1</strong> (1 kΩ) is the input resistor, <strong>R2</strong> (10 kΩ) is the feedback resistor</li><li>The + input is grounded, so the - input is a virtual ground</li><li><strong>V1:</strong> 0.5 V, 1 kHz sine input</li></ul></div><div class="ch-formula">Vout / Vin = - R2 / R1 = <strong>-10</strong></div></div>
    </div>
    </div></foreignObject></g>